 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely (inaudible) to this. Okay. Thirdlove.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So let's start with Thirdlove. Yes, so this is one of the top sellers. I think everyone can hear me now, right? Can you hear me? Okay. Anyway, this one is great. It comes in half sizes. Super innovative. This has nearly 11,000 five star reviews. And the reason for that is it fits every body. And, you know, women don't really realize that sometimes you're between sizes.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRAS: FOR EVERY DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CLASSIC T-SHIRT BRA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIRDLOVE $72\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So this was super innovative. They're also, if you buy this pink bra, they're donating a dollar to breast cancer charities.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wonderful.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Up to $10,000. So it's a great thing to get involved in. And this one we're seeing is great for everyday wear.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Everyday wear.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's their classic bra. You will not go wrong with that one at all.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Excellent. What do we have here, Lori?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOP NOW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOODMORNINGAMERICA.COM\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, next we're here with \uc2 Spanx\uc2 . This one is called, ready for this? Bra-llelujah. So what we love about this one...\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRAS: FOR FULL COVERAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPANXSMOOTH BRA-LLELUJAH!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPANX $68\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Bra-llelujah.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...is it's super comfortable, has that front closure snap there. And, you know, \uc2 Spanx\uc2  is known for that light compression, keeping everything really well supported. And feel the back of this bra, Rebecca.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, this is so nice.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So that's actually made of hosiery. And because of that, it's really soft, it's really smooth. People...\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And you're not going to have the marks in the back.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Exactly. And our producer, Carolyn, made a good point. She said when you lean back, it's just so comfortable.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Because there's nothing back there to snap. So these are really great as well. We love bra-llelujah. Okay. And then we're gonna move on to fuller figure. So we actually found this one on Amazon. And it has over 50,000 five star reviews. Women with fuller figures have told us that either they have to sacrifice comfort for support or vice versa. Something's very supportive but it's also very restrictive. What people love about this one is the comfort factor. And they felt like they got a lift and a lot of support. And the size range here is incredible. It goes up to a band size of 48 and a cup size of H. So you get a lot of variety there, and the best part about this? $25.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRAS: LARGE BUSTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VANITY FAIR BACK SMOOTHING MINIMIZER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMAZON $24.99\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) $25 on Amazon. Okay.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, really incredible. Okay. We have to get to this because everybody was talking about this.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Workout. Yes.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So this is actually not, well, you can use it to work out.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You don't have to work out in this.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It's everyday or workout, but it's a posture bra. Now you may have heard about this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRAS: POSTURE BRA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWER BRA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORME $185\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes. I need this.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Because it went viral when Taylor Swift wore it when she was rehearsing for her Eras Tour. So people were, had a lot of questions. Does it really work? This was actually developed by an orthopedic surgeon. And he, you know, he made it so that women can have better posture. It was in honor of his mom, who was suffering from cancer. And he wanted to help her with her alignment. It's great. If you feel it, you can feel the fibers in here. They're very supportive.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're, help you keep your shoulders back. Every, and like I said, you can wear it every day. You can wear it for working out. And if you buy their set, 50 percent of their proceeds will go to various breast cancer charities as well for the next two weeks.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) 50 percent?\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But this thing is really incredible. Everybody on set, all the women were like, can I try that out? Can I try that out? It's good enough for Taylor Swift.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're also thinking, wait, how's my posture right now?\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) How's my posture. But it really, I tried one of these on and it really will keep you, you know, really aligned and your shoulders back. I am obsessed with this and I am a believer.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We believe in you, Lori.\par \par \uc2 LORI BERGAMOTTO (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, thank you.\par \par \uc2 REBECCA JARVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Looking great as always. So excellent. Thank you. And we've got even more of your bra picks right on our website. And coming up, our Ray of Sunshine surprise at a Brooklyn block party. Stay with us. There will be dancing.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROMOTIONAL CONSIDERATION PROVIDED BY...\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241023eka40000s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MELANIA TRUMP'S DEFENSE OF ABORTION RIGHTS FORMER FIRST LADY REPORTEDLY CALLS IT A "FUNDAMENTAL RIGHT" IN NEW MEMOIR\b0\par\par\uc2 647 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELENE'S DESTRUCTION\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE, HELEN, NORTH, CAROLINA, BIDEN, TROOPS, HARRIS, MORGAN\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ELECTION, CASE, SMITH, BIDEN, JAN. 6, PENCE, RIOTERS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , MEMOIR, ABORTION, RIGHTS, SCOTUS, ROE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Terry Moran. Thank you so much for your reporting. We're gonna turn now to Melania Trump's defense of abortion rights. The former first lady reportedly wrote her upcoming memoir that abortion is a, quote, "woman's fundamental right," end quote, in opposition to her husband's views. Rachel Scott joins us with more. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MELANIA TRUMP'S DEFENSE OF ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER FIRST LADY REPORTEDLY CALLS IT A "FUNDAMENTAL RIGHT" IN NEW MEMOIR\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael, good morning to you. Yes, Melania Trump reportedly at odds with her husband on the key issue of abortion rights. This news coming in the final stretch as the Trump campaign is working overtime trying to appeal to female voters.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, in the final weeks of the 2024 campaign and just as her husband is trying to appeal to female voters, a report that Melania Trump is publicly breaking with her husband on abortion rights. In her upcoming memoir, the former first lady reportedly writing, "Why should anyone other than the woman herself have the power to determine what she does with her own body? A woman's fundamental right of individual liberty, to her own life, grants her the authority to terminate her pregnancy if she wishes," adding that a woman's autonomy should be free from any intervention for pressure from the Government, and reportedly writing she has carried this belief throughout her entire adult life."\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER FIRST LADY REPORTEDLY DIFFERS FROM THE FORMER PRESIDENT ON KEY ISSUE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The excerpts were obtained exclusively by "The Guardian," have not been verified by ABC News. It's a sharp contrast to the former president, who has reportedly bragged about nominating three of the Supreme Court justices who over turned Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM APRIL 12\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (2024 REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL NOMINEE)\par \par \uc2 We gave it back to the states and the states are working very brilliantly. In some cases Conservative, in some not Conservative. But they're working. And it's working the way it's supposed to.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATES BANNING OR SEVERELY RESTRICTING ACCESS TO ABORTION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Twenty states have banned or severely restricted access to abortion. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  putting the issue front and center.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM SEPTEMBER 29\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 One in three women in America lives in a state with a Trump abortion ban. Many with no exceptions even for rape and incest. It is immoral. Immoral.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Melania Trump has only made a handful of campaign appearances this cycle.\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIP FROM MARCH 19\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXT OF DIALOGUE\par \par \uc2 REPORTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Are you going to return to the campaign trail with your husband?\par \par \uc2 MELANIA TRUMP (FORMER FIRST LADY)\par \par \uc2 Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But her comments come as the Republican ticket is making an all-out appeal to women who are concerned about abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This morning the Trump campaign declined to comment. The former president is behind Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  when it comes to likely female voters. And he tried to change his messaging on the campaign trail, vowing to be a protector for women. And, of course, it was days ago that his running mate, Senator JD Vance, said that Republicans have to do more to earn the trust back from Americans and female voters on the key issue of reproductive rights, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241022eka30002w\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 URGENT RELIEF EFFORTS; OVER 200 DEATHS INSIDE THE RACE TO GET SUPPLIES TO THE STORM ZONE\b0\par\par\uc2 635 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NICHOLS, VERDICT, BEAN, HALEY, SMITH, WELLS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MELANIA TRUMP DEFENDS ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, CHENEY, SPRINGSTEEN, ENDORSEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHENEY CAMPAIGNING WITH HARRIS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, SHORES, SCHUMACHER, INGRAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT RELIEF EFFORTS; OVER 200 DEATHS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Next, tonight, Hurricane Helene, now the deadliest hurricane since Katrina. More than 200 people now confirmed dead, hundreds still unaccounted for. And the remarkable new images still emerging after this storm.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A camper van plunging over a waterfall in a rushing river. This is in Virginia, just extraordinary. And tonight now, an investigation after floodwaters tore through a factory and a parking lot. What workers were told as the waters were rising. They're looking into this. At least two workers were killed in Tennessee. National Guard troops delivering water in hard-hit Asheville, North Carolina. And with so many roads impassable, mules are now being used to deliver medicine and supplies. This is in Black Mountain, North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ABC's Morgan Norwood again from North Carolina.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: INSIDE THE RACE TO GET SUPPLIES TO THE STORM ZONE\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, the staggering human toll from Hurricane Helene. More than 200 killed, countless communities crippled. In Asheville, the North Carolina National Guard working 24/7 to get those supplies out into the field.\par \par \uc2 FIRST LIEUTENANT JUSTIN SHORES (ENGINEERING OFFICER NC NATIONAL GUARD)\par \par \uc2 We've been running supplies to fire stations, homeless shelters, schools where they have temporary airfield set up just to get the supplies out, so they can distribute those out to communities, just to get them to people in need who are stranded or just low on supplies.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But with hundreds of roads unpassable, troops can only go so far. Outside Asheville, in Swannanoa, we found volunteers using pack mules to get insulin over those last rugged steps up the mountain to families in need.\par \par \uc2 AMANDA SCHUMACHER (VOLUNTEER MOUNTAIN MULE PACKERS)\par \par \uc2 Thank you, guys, for clearing the path.\par \par \uc2 AMANDA SCHUMACHER (VOLUNTEER MOUNTAIN MULE PACKERS)\par \par \uc2 You know, to be able to put four or five mules in a row, you know, with one person leading them, you know, they're able to carry 150 pounds each to get supplies, which is more effective.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Meanwhile, in Tennessee, the attorney general launching a criminal investigation into the owner of the Impact Plastics factory in Erwin. Videos posted to social media showing Helene's floodwaters swallowing cars in the factory's parking lot. Two employees did not survive. Jacob Ingram among some workers alleging permission to leave the facility came too late.\par \par \uc2 JACOB INGRAM (EMPLOYEE IMPACT PLASTICS)\par \par \uc2 I went and asked one of the higher ups if we could leave, and they told us to not to leave yet, that they had to go make sure that it was okay for us to leave with another higher up.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The company says it will cooperate fully, writing, "At no time were employees told they would be fired if they left the facility." And tonight, we're learning more about the victims. Grandparents Jerry and Marcia Savage were teenage sweethearts, married more than 50 years. They were killed when a tree fell on their Beech Island, South Carolina, home. Their son says they were found in each other's arms, in a final embrace.\par \par \uc2 MORGAN NORWOOD (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, David, back here in western North Carolina, they are still searching tonight. The Buncombe County sheriff says more than 200 people still unaccounted for. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thinking about all of those families through this storm zone. Thank you again tonight, Morgan.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241007eka30002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DOCKWORKER STRIKE AGREEMENT TO SUSPEND STRIKE UNTIL JANUARY 15\b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NICHOLS, VERDICT, BEAN, HALEY, SMITH, WELLS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MELANIA TRUMP DEFENDS ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, CHENEY, SPRINGSTEEN, ENDORSEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHENEY CAMPAIGNING WITH HARRIS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, SHORES, SCHUMACHER, INGRAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT RELIEF EFFORTS; OVER 200 DEATHS\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKERS, STRIKE, AGREEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, there's also breaking news at this hour involving that dock workers strike that has crippled shipping all along the East Coast and the Gulf, in fact. There is late word coming in at this hour that the union is suspending the strike until at least January 15th. ABC's Elizabeth Schulze live with us tonight. Elizabeth, what have you learned?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOCKWORKER STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AGREEMENT TO SUSPEND STRIKE UNTIL JANUARY 15\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, sources familiar with these negotiations tell us that the union and the shipping industry group have reached a tentative agreement that will suspend this strike until January 15th.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This agreement covers wages. Both sides would then return to the negotiating table to resolve their outstanding issues in January. We've seen this strike stretch three days, 47,000 dockworkers walked off the job for the first time in nearly 50 years. And shipping at more than a dozen ports all along the eastern gulf coast has been at a standstill.\par \par \uc2 ELIZABETH SCHULZE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Those shipments should now be able to resume. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, hopefully that's relief for both the workers and the millions of Americans who are bracing for higher prices in the coming weeks. Elizabeth Schulze with the breaking news. Thank you, Elizabeth.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241007eka30002y\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE INDEX\b0\par\par\uc2 216 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NICHOLS, VERDICT, BEAN, HALEY, SMITH, WELLS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MELANIA TRUMP DEFENDS ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, CHENEY, SPRINGSTEEN, ENDORSEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHENEY CAMPAIGNING WITH HARRIS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, SHORES, SCHUMACHER, INGRAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT RELIEF EFFORTS; OVER 200 DEATHS\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKERS, STRIKE, AGREEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, HEZBOLLAH, LEBANON, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL TARGETS BEIRUT; AIRSTRIKE KILLS AMERICAN\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, TRIAL, SHOOTING, CANCUN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROSECUTORS TO REVIEW MENENDEZ CASE\par \par \uc2 BROOKS, LAWSUIT, CLARK, \uc2 WNBA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To "The Index" of other news. Garth Brooks is facing a new lawsuit accusing him of sexual assault and misconduct.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A hair and makeup artist claims he assaulted her many times while working for him in 2019. He has previously denied all allegations.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Indiana Fever star Caitlin Clark has been named \uc2 WNBA\uc2  rookie of the year.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She led all rookies in points, assists, and steals. Her teammates celebrating when she got the call.\par \par \uc2 WNBA OFFICIAL (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Congratulations, you are the 2024 Kia WNBA rookie of the year.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Clark also helping to lead the league to record ticket sales. When we come back here tonight, the wedding surprise. After the "I do," one more question, in a moment here.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241007eka300031\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MELANIA TRUMP DEFENDS ABORTION RIGHTS FMR. FIRST LADY: ABORTION IS A 'WOMAN'S FUNDAMENTAL RIGHT'\b0\par\par\uc2 678 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NICHOLS, VERDICT, BEAN, HALEY, SMITH, WELLS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MELANIA TRUMP DEFENDS ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Meantime, we turn now to former First Lady Melania Trump, in a major break with her husband, taking a stand to support abortion rights. Reportedly writing in her new memoir that abortion is a woman's fundamental right, and saying in social media that there is no room for compromise when it comes to this essential right. But in excerpts and video released so far, Melania Trump makes no mention of her husband, former President Trump, taking credit for appointing the three justices who helped the Supreme Court overturn Roe. Tonight, the former president's response just in. And here's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FMR. FIRST LADY: ABORTION IS A 'WOMAN'S FUNDAMENTAL RIGHT'\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in battleground Michigan, rallying his supporters, but making no mention of the surprising new headline from his wife. Former First Lady Melania Trump now staking out a very different position from her husband on the critical issue of abortion. In excerpts from her new memoir published by "The Guardian," the former first lady declaring herself a lifelong supporter of abortion rights, writing, "Restricting a woman's right to choose whether to terminate an unwanted pregnancy is the same as denying her control over her own body." Mrs. Trump, who rarely speaks out on issues, then releasing this promotional video just 33 days before the election.\par \par \uc2 MELANIA TRUMP (FORMER FIRST LADY)\par \par \uc2 There is no room for compromise when it comes to this essential right that all women possess from birth, individual freedom. What does "My body, my choice" really mean?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to the book excerpts, which ABC News has not confirmed, the former first lady writes, "A woman's fundamental right of individual liberty, to her own life, grants her the authority to terminate her pregnancy if she wishes." But in none of the published excerpts did Mrs. Trump address her husband's key role in eliminating a woman's constitutional right to an abortion. The former president has often boasted of appointing three of the Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe versus Wade.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Nobody has ever done more for right to life than \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . I put three Supreme Court justices, who all voted, and they got something that they've been fighting for for 64 years.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Throughout his presidency, Trump proclaimed himself a staunch opponent of abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I'm proud to be the most pro-life president in American history.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, with the election fast approaching and Trump struggling to win over some women voters, he insists he wanted the matter of abortion returned to the states. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says, don't be fooled.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 He intended for them to undo the protections of Roe v. Wade. And as he intended, they did. Now, in more than 20 states, there is a Trump abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  responding to his wife's new words.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We spoke about it. And I said, you have to write what you believe. I'm not going to tell you what to do. You have to write what you believe.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Again, David, none of the passages that have been released so far of Melania Trump's the book make any mention of Roe versus Wade being overturned, or her husband's role in appointing three of the Supreme Court justices who ultimately supported that decision. She did not speak out then, but she is making her position known now, 33 days out from the November election, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott on the campaign trail. Rachel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241007eka30002v\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 AMERICA STRONG THE WEDDING SURPRISE\b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 NICHOLS, VERDICT, BEAN, HALEY, SMITH, WELLS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MELANIA TRUMP DEFENDS ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, CHENEY, SPRINGSTEEN, ENDORSEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CHENEY CAMPAIGNING WITH HARRIS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, SHORES, SCHUMACHER, INGRAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT RELIEF EFFORTS; OVER 200 DEATHS\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKERS, STRIKE, AGREEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, HEZBOLLAH, LEBANON, IRAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL TARGETS BEIRUT; AIRSTRIKE KILLS AMERICAN\par \par \uc2 MENENDEZ, TRIAL, SHOOTING, CANCUN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PROSECUTORS TO REVIEW MENENDEZ CASE\par \par \uc2 BROOKS, LAWSUIT, CLARK, \uc2 WNBA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 WEDDING, ADOPTION, MAPLES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: #AMERICASTRONG\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Finally tonight here, the moment after the "I dos" that was just as moving.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GATLINBURG, TN\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, in Gatlinburg, Tennessee, the emotional surprise at this wedding that had everyone, especially the groom, in tears. Erin and Matt Maples getting married after years together, blending their families. Among them, Erin's 12-year-old daughter Kylie. She and Matt bonded over the years. She would eventually tell her mother that she hoped that Matt would adopt her one day. Right before the wedding, mom and daughter came up with an idea, that right after the "I dos," Kylie would hold up this handmade sign. "You didn't give me life, life gave me you. Thank you for always loving me as your own, but I have a question." The other side reading, "Will you be my dad forever?" This is the moment.\par \par \uc2 KYLIE (DAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 Will you be my dad forever?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, that daughter Kylie telling us, "I was so nervous until I saw Matt's face light up. Then I felt much better. When Matt was reading the sign, he started tearing up, and I knew that made him the happiest in the world." And that new forever father tonight, Matt, who was adopted himself, telling us, "It was a really special moment, the fact a child wants you to be their father. I was thinking, I just hoped I would be able to give her the love that my adopted parents gave me." Tonight, the newlyweds and their new forever family, grateful.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, what a beautiful family. We sure needed that tonight. I'm David Muir. I'll see you right back here tomorrow. Good night.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241007eka300032\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\b0\par\par\uc2 566 \uc2 words\par \uc2 3 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the verdict just in in the police beating death of Tyre Nichols. The future of three former Memphis officers in the jury's hands. What they have just decided. Also, tonight, Melania Trump in a major break with her husband on abortion rights, saying it's a woman's fundamental right. And what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  just said about this. Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  at this hour appearing with \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 . And Bruce Springsteen endorsing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . And tonight, the developing headline involving the Menendez brothers.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VERDICT IN TYRE NICHOLS BEATING CASE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 First, tonight, this verdict just in in the police beating death of Tyre Nichols following a traffic stop. Three former Memphis police officers accused of violating his civil rights. Federal prosecutors say the officers laughed and bragged about beating him, saying they never called medics in order to protect themselves. What the jury just decided and we'll go live to the courthouse.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MELANIA TRUMP DEFENDS ABORTION RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, former First Lady Melania Trump and that break with her husband, taking a stand to support abortion rights. Reportedly writing in her new memoir, "Abortion is a woman's fundamental right." But in excerpts and video released so far, Melania Trump makes no mention of her husband, President Trump, taking credit for appointing the three justices who helped the Supreme Court overturn Roe in this country. Tonight, the former president's response just in.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS CAMPAIGNING WITH LIZ CHENEY\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Meantime, at this hour, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  campaigning in Wisconsin with former Republican Congresswoman \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2 , the daughter of former Vice President \uc2 Dick Cheney\uc2 , a former Republican leader on Capitol Hill. Both \uc2 Liz Cheney\uc2  and her father have endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELENE DEATHS TOP 200; URGENT RELIEF EFFORT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The death toll from Hurricane Helene rising. More than 200 dead now, including a couple married more than 50 years. Grandparents found together in their home. Tonight, the National Guard on the ground, mules now being used to get through areas with supplies because vehicles still cannot get through in some regions.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACKLOG OF CARGO SHIPS GROWING\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The economy tonight. And the dockworkers strike is now in its third day. Could there be more than 100 container ships waiting off the East Coast and the Gulf by tomorrow? And what this could mean for the prices you pay.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MENENDEZ BROTHERS BOMBSHELL\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The breaking headline tonight. The notorious murder trial of Lyle and Erik Menendez. The brothers sentenced to life in prison without parole for killing their parents. What the Los Angeles DA is now suggesting.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY ATTACK AT POPULAR RESORT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, tourists horrified in Cancun. Gunmen storming the beach, killing someone. The escape then on a jet ski.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GARTH BROOKS LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Tonight, the new lawsuit filed against country music star Garth Brooks. A hairstylist and makeup artist accusing him of sexual assault. And tonight, who is the \uc2 WNBA\uc2 's rookie of the year? The cheers when they heard her name.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT WITH DAVID MUIR\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 From ABC News world headquarters in New York, this is "World News Tonight with David Muir."\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241007eka30002t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HIGH-STAKES VP DEBATE SHOWDOWN TIM WALZ & JD VANCE FACE OFF WITH PRESIDENTIAL RACE NECK-AND-NECK\b0\par\par\uc2 869 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP DEBATE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 DEBATE, WALZ, VANCE, JAN 6TH, ABORTION, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 WALZ, VANCE, DEBATE, TAKEAWAYS, CAMPAIGNS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, MISSILES, RETALIATION, CRATERS, TERRORISTS\par \par \uc2 IRAN, MISSILES, ATTACK, ISRAEL, TROOPS\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, MISSILES, RESPONSE, ESCALATION\par \par \uc2 HELENE, MISSING, SEARCH, DEATHS, BIDEN, DAMAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OCTOBER HEAT WAVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 COMBS, ALLEGATIONS, BUZBEE, LAWSUITS, CHARGES\par \par \uc2 AMOS, "GOOD TIMES", "ROOTS", LEGACY, TRIBUTES\par \par \uc2 MICROSOFT\uc2 , AI, CO-PILOT, QUI, EMOTIONAL\par \par \uc2 WNBA, PLAYOFFS, LYNX, SUN, \uc2 LIBERTY\uc2 , ACES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW WARNING FOR PARENTS\par \par \uc2 WALZ, VANCE, DEBATE, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First look at the top stories breaking at 8. We start with last night's vice presidential debate. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 /J.D. Vance. 34 days until the final votes. Let's bring Rachel Scott back. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP DEBATE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: IRAN MISSILE ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE PORT STRIKE\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George. Good morning to you. And the stakes here were unusually high. 34 days out from the election, this race is now locked in a dead heat. And with no other debates scheduled, it is the vice presidential candidates that got the final word.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES VP DEBATE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIM WALZ & JD VANCE FACE OFF WITH PRESIDENTIAL RACE NECK-AND-NECK\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, in what is likely the last debate before the November election, the two vice presidential candidates sparring over the results of the last election, with Senator J.D. Vance refusing to admit his running mate, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , lost.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR TIM WALZ (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 He is still saying he didn't lose the election. I would just ask that. Did he lose the 2020 election?\par \par \uc2 SENATOR J.D. VANCE (OHIO)\par \par \uc2 Tim, I'm focused on the future. Did \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  censor Americans from speaking their mind in the wake of the 2020 COVID situation?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR TIM WALZ (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 That is a damning, that is a damning non-answer.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Minnesota governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  challenging Vance to admit Trump was defeated, pointing out Trump's former vice president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , wasn't on the debate stage because he stood up to him on January 6th.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR TIM WALZ (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 Where is the firewall with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ? Where is the firewall if he knows he can do anything, including taking an election and his vice president is not going to stand up to it? That's what we are asking you, America? Will you stand up? Will you keep your oath of office even if the president doesn't?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Much of the debate was civil and cordial, focused on policy, from immigration to abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR J.D. VANCE (OHIO)\par \par \uc2 That is, I think...\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR TIM WALZ (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 That's not true.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR J.D. VANCE (OHIO)\par \par \uc2 ...whether you're pro-choice or pro abortion...\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR TIM WALZ (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 That's not (inaudible).\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Both asked to explain their past comments. Walz asked about false claims he made that he was in Hong Kong during the democracy protests back in 1989.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR TIM WALZ (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 I'm a knucklehead at times. Alls I said on this was is I got there that summer and misspoke on this.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Vance pressed on his own words from 2016, claiming Trump was unfit for the nation's highest office.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR J.D. VANCE (OHIO)\par \par \uc2 I disagreed with the President, but I've also been extremely open about the fact that I was wrong about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The other major issue, abortion rights. Walz placing the blame squarely on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for sweeping abortion restrictions in nearly two dozen states.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR TIM WALZ (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 How can we as a nation say that your life and your rights, as basic as the right to control your own body, is determined on geography?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has bragged about appointing three of the Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe versus Wade, but Vance acknowledging Republicans have to do better on this issue.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR J.D. VANCE (OHIO)\par \par \uc2 My party, we've got to do so much better of a job at earning the American people's trust back on this issue, where they, frankly, just don't trust us. And I think that's one of the things that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and I are endeavoring to do.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So no personal attacks or insults. This debate was civil at times. The two candidates even acknowledge where they have common ground. It's likely the last marquee event before the November election. This morning, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  once again making it clear he's not interested in another debate. But, guys, look, we've covered so many of these now. The last two, the tone was just so different this time around. Civil is not a word that we used to describe those last two debates.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) No, no. But we're 34 days away. 34 days away. Rachel, thank you, as always.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241019eka20000g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HIGH STAKES VP DEBATE SHOWDOWN TIM WALZ & JD VANCE FACE OFF WITH PRESIDENTIAL RACE NECK AND NECK\b0\par\par\uc2 1,057 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP DEBATE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 DEBATE, WALZ, VANCE, JAN 6TH, ABORTION, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we begin with last night's high stakes vice presidential debate. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and JD Vance faced off with the race between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  neck and neck. Mary Bruce and \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2  are standing by with the reaction. But first Rachel Scott is here to start us off with the highlights. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH STAKES VP DEBATE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TIM WALZ & JD VANCE FACE OFF WITH PRESIDENTIAL RACE NECK AND NECK\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, good morning to you, Michael. Look, no name calling, no personal insults, but there were sharp divides over policy, and the stakes were unusually high here. We are just 34 days out from the November election. This race is locked in a dead heat, and with no other debates scheduled, it is the vice presidential candidates that got the final word.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, in what is likely the last debate before the November election, the two vice presidential candidates sparring over the results of the last election, with Senator J.D. Vance refusing to admit his running mate \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  lost.\par \par \uc2 GOV TIM WALZ (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 This was a threat to our democracy in a way that we had not seen. And it manifested itself because of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's inability to say, he is still saying he didn't lose the election. I would just ask that, did he lose the 2020 election?\par \par \uc2 SEN JD VANCE (REP) (OHIO)\par \par \uc2 Tim, I'm focused on the future. Did \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  censor Americans from speaking their mind in the wake of the 2020 COVID situation?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH STAKES VP DEBATE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WALZ & VANCE GO HEAD TO HEAD OVER ECONOMY, ABORTION, BORDER & JAN 6TH\par \par \uc2 GOV TIM WALZ (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 That is a damning, that is a damning non-answer.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Minnesota Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  challenging Vance to admit Trump was defeated, pointing out Trump's former vice president, \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2 , wasn't on the debate stage because he stood up to him on January 6th.\par \par \uc2 GOV TIM WALZ (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 That's why \uc2 Mike Pence\uc2  isn't on this stage. What I'm concerned about is where is the firewall with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ? Where is the firewall if he knows he can do anything, including taking an election and his vice president's not going to stand to it. That's what we're asking you, America? Will you stand up? Will you keep your oath of office even if the President doesn't?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Much of the debate was civil and cordial, focused on policy, from immigration to abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 SEN JD VANCE (REP) (OHIO)\par \par \uc2 That is I think whether you are pro choice\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Walz got off to a shaky start, appearing being nervous, at one point mixing up Israel and Iran.\par \par \uc2 GOV TIM WALZ (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 The expansion of Israel and its proxies is an absolute fundamental necessity for the United States steady leadership there.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Both candidates asked to explain their past comments. Walz asked about false claims he made that he was in Hong Kong during the democracy protests back in 1989.\par \par \uc2 GOV TIM WALZ (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 I'm a knucklehead at times. All I said on this was is I got there that summer and misspoke on this. So I will just, that's what I've said. So I was in Hong Kong and China during the democracy protest went in. And from that I learned a lot of what needed to be in governance.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Vance pressed on his own words from 2016 claiming Trump was unfit for the nation's highest office.\par \par \uc2 SEN JD VANCE (REP) (OHIO)\par \par \uc2 Sometimes, of course, I've disagree with the President. But I've also been extremely open about the fact that I was wrong about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Vance was more measured than he has been on the campaign trail after amplifying false claims that Haitian migrants in his home state of Ohio were eating neighborhood pets, the Ohio senator now shying away from it on the debate stage. But after a tense exchange on the exchange, the moderators muting the candidates microphones. Vance cut off.\par \par \uc2 MODERATOR (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Gentlemen, the audience can't hear you because your mics are cut. We have so much we want to get to. Thank you for explaining the legal process.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The other major issue, abortion rights, Walz placing the blame squarely on \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for sweeping abortion restrictions in nearly two states, telling the stories of women impacted by the bans.\par \par \uc2 GOV TIM WALZ (DEM) (MINNESOTA)\par \par \uc2 How can we as a nation say that your life and your rights, as basic as the right to control your own body, is determined on geography?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has bragged about appointing three of the Supreme Court Justices who overturned Roe versus Wade. But Vance acknowledging Republicans have to do better on this issue.\par \par \uc2 SEN JD VANCE (REP) (OHIO)\par \par \uc2 My party, we've got to do so much better of a job at earning the American people's trust back on this issue where they frankly just don't trust us. and I think that's one of the things that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and I are endeavoring to do. I want us, as a Republican Party, to be pro-family in the fullest sense of the word.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The Trump campaign trying to make some in roads with likely female voters. So this debate was civil. At times these two candidates even acknowledged where they have common ground. It was a much different tone from the last two presidential debates.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is holding firm. He made it clear again he is not interested in another debate with Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , calling it too late even though he has participated in debates in late October in both 2016 and 2020, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241019eka200002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 COUNTDOWN TO THE VICE PRESIDENTIAL DEBATE THE RACE TO THE WHITE HOUSE\b0\par\par\uc2 9,688 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Special Report\par \uc2 ABSR\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 (c) Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SPECIAL REPORT\par \par \uc2 DEBATE, WALZ, VANCE, BIDEN, HARRIS, TRUMP, MIDDLE EAST, POLLING, VOTERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening, everyone. We are just one hour away from tonight's high-stakes vice presidential debate between Minnesota Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  and Ohio Senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 . We will carry the debate live right here on ABC. The running mates for Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  about to take center stage here in New York. Each candidate set to make their case to the American voters with just 35 days now until Election Day. Of course, early voting already underway.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight's news overseas, of course, likely to be a key issue with this evening's debate, the major escalation of violence in the Middle East. Iran launching a massive ballistic missile attack on Israel, more than 200 missiles, the largest missile attack on Israel ever. It comes as retaliation for Israel's killing of \uc2 Hezbollah\uc2 's leader in Beirut. Tonight, after Iran's attack, Israel now vowing to strike back. Governor Walz and Senator Vance likely to face questions on the crisis in the Middle East, and, of course, the many issues right here at home.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Earlier today, we saw Vice President Harris in the Situation Room with President Biden monitoring the events unfolding in real time. She then spoke before the cameras about her steadfast support of Israel. Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Wisconsin today, blaming the escalation in the Middle East on Biden and Harris. Walz and Vance coming face to face tonight amid an extremely tight race, especially in the all-important battleground states that, as we all know, will decide this election. In those key seven swing states, the difference between \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , in many cases, less than a point. The Vice Presidential candidates expected to be pressed on the economy, inflation, abortion, and immigration.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , a relative unknown on the national stage before joining the Harris ticket, will be making his case to America tonight. Sources telling ABC News, during the vetting process, he told \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  he was a, quote, "bad debater." But again, the question tonight, and we'll talk about this here, is that all part of lowering expectations, really on both sides, we'll see coming up. JD Vance will come to the stage after igniting a firestorm of sorts with false claims that he made about Haitian immigrants in Springfield, Ohio. We'll go to Ohio later on in this primetime special.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight's showdown may be the last time the two campaigns square off before the election. We have our entire Powerhouse political team right here tonight, so let's jump right in. Great to have everybody, the usual suspects right here with me tonight. \uc2 Jon Karl\uc2 , let's start right off with you. Late reporting here tonight from both campaigns, and this, this talk of lowering expectations, both of these men have been in politics for a long time. They know what they're doing.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, give me a break. When they say that Governor Walz is nervous, he's worried he may let \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  down. He's somebody that doesn't have much experience with this. He's been a politician, he's been a - political candidate some for two decades. He's done more than a dozen debates. He's actually quite good at them. But look, David, the big picture here is that there's a general perception that vice presidential debates don't make that much of a difference. But both of these campaigns, both of these candidates know that this debate has the potential to be decisive. This race is so tight.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You know, JD Vance has had a rather relatively disastrous rollout as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's running mate. He's viewed unpopularly by most Americans. This is his chance, really his only chance to change this. And Walz, he has done really no, he's been exposed to no questions since he became \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' running mate, no real interviews. This is the first time many Americans will get a chance to see him outside of what we saw at the convention.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Really, that part of it is, is truly remarkable. But a quick follow-up to you, Jon, because you interviewed JD Vance.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Obviously, he was selected by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in part because of his capabilities out there on the trail as an attack dog for \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . He was very tough in reacting to you in that interview. He knew the questions that were coming his way. And when you talk about Governor Walz for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , he's the one who came out with this sort of "weird" moniker in describing the Trump-Vance ticket. So, really, both of these guys have been out there as the attack dogs for the, the people at the top of the ticket.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, he was chosen because, really Walz, he was the most affective surrogate for, for, for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , and for \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  before Harris became the nominee. And JD Vance is very slick, very good at this. He is a shrewd debater. Interview after interview, no matter how hard the questions are that you throw at him, he diverts, he comes back and he turns to, to the points that he wants to make. I expect you'll see that tonight.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Fifty-five minutes, but who's counting? Fifty-five minutes until the Vice Presidential Debate. We're gonna carry it live right here on ABC, so you won't miss a moment of it. But we'll continue with our team and their sort of inside reporting. Mary, you've been talking with your sources inside the Harris campaign. How do they feel going into tonight? And as we established here with Jon, they are trying to lower expectations.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They certainly are. Look, behind the scenes tonight, I'm told that in preparing for this, \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  really views this as a chance for him to take on the mantle at the top of the ticket. That he's going into this trying to debate for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , to keep the momentum of her strong debate performance going. And that means his goal here is, in many ways, to look past JD Vance and try to bring the conversation back to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  as much as possible. This is also a chance, of course, for him to introduce himself to many voters. Let's be honest, you know, just a couple weeks ago most Americans had never heard of Governor \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So he has been intensely preparing, doing those mock debate sessions. And yes, we know he's, he's fighting a bit of nerves. They've been trying to lower those expectations. Sources are quick to note that, you know, the debate stage is not his strong suit. He's more comfortable working a rope line. And yes, we do know that he, in the vetting process, told \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  that he's a, quote, "bad debater." But let's be honest and make no mistake here.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Past that, you know, Midwestern, folksy dad persona of his, he is a very skilled politician. He knows what he is doing and he knows how to land a punch. And he is going to be the \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  we have seen out on the campaign trail, but expect that now, you know, in a different format. And as you mentioned, you know, he is the one, of course, who coined that new go-to attack line that Trump and Vance are just weird.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But I've got to ask, Mary, isn't it gonna be more difficult to get under JD Vance's skin? A lot of folks looked...\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...very closely at \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 's performance. People at home can judge whether she did well or not. But, but it was clear that she set out to try to get under \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's skin in the Presidential Debate. JD Vance, I, I would gather might be a little more difficult to do that to.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They know that that kind of needling that we saw at our debate that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  really was intent on getting underneath, underneath Trump's skin. That doesn't work as well here. JD Vance isn't as susceptible to those kinds of attacks. He's a little too slick for that, as Jon was saying. And that in part is why that's not his goal. He's going to try and bring it back to the top of the ticket, bring it back to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  instead of focusing on trying to get under Vance's skin.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's swing it over to Rachel Scott who covers the Trump campaign, also has some late reporting for us tonight. And Rachel, I was struck by the fact that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was calling \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  a moron, said he couldn't, he couldn't debate, right? But then you've got JD Vance out there saying \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  is a great debater, so you had competing messages from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and JD Vance. But they too are trying to lower expectations going into tonight, as well.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, just when Senator JD Vance is trying to lower expectations, leave it to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  himself to sort of, just raise them entirely. Look, I think what Mary just reported here is going to be music to, to the \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  campaign's ears because they want this to be about the top of the ticket. It may be \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  that's gonna be standing next to Senator JD Vance on that debate stage. But make no mistake about it. JD Vance is gonna bring this back to Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They are in a race to try to define her. They're looking at the polls, they're seeing that voters still have questions about her. So, expect them to try to use Walz's record to cast Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  as Liberal. I'm also told that, yes, he's been doing these formal mock debates as well, as \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  has been doing. But he's also preparing to take questions on controversial comments that he himself has made, that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has made, even his own past statements about the former president. Remember, this is someone that he once called reprehensible. He's gonna be prepared to defend those comments and defend the former president's record on the debate stage.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's talk a little bit about those comments so that people at home can be watching for this. You're, you're saying JD Vance is fully prepared to, to hear about, you know, the eating of dogs and cats, for example, in, in that town in Ohio.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Also the comments about, you know, "cat ladies" or, or, or single women or, or that people who don't have children might not have the voting power perhaps as people who are part of a family unit. All of those lines, those moments along the way in this campaign, he's prepared to take on tonight?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And these are headlines that Republicans did not want to see when it was announced that JD Vance was gonna be selected as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's running mate. But yes, he made those comments suggesting that Democrats without kids or childless cat ladies, he even made comments suggesting that people without kids should have less voting power or less power at the voting box than people with, with kids. And so, I am told that in these formal mock debate sessions, he has been prepared to answer questions on all of those subjects, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Rachel Scott with us here as well. I've noticed a serenity and calmness to Linsey Davis here tonight.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Isn't it, isn't it nice not having to moderate the debate, and instead...\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Where's my cigarette?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I know, exactly, just to cover the debate instead with the rest of the team. But, you know, another sort of elephant in the room here is that the country doesn't really know these guys that well.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Right.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) They're both are Midwestern dads, but they're so different when you start to learn a little bit more about them.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This is essentially tonight big dad energy versus "Hillbilly Elegy." And we talk about Tim Scott, a relatively unknown Midwestern governor...\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , yeah.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, yeah.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I have Rachel Scott in my head. \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2 , a, a relatively unknown Midwestern governor, but people who do know him know him for his flannel shirts and his folksy style. This is a guy who was born in rural America in a county in Nebraska that boasts more cows than people. He's often said that there were 25 people in his high school graduating class, 12 of them were his cousins. He went and served in the National Guard for 24 years, started out as a high school social studies teacher and football coach, then turned Congressman, ultimately, governor of Minnesota, but many people affectionately still call him, as does \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , Coach Walz.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Many people will remember seeing some of the members of that high school state championship team that he coached that went on stage during the DNC this summer. That's also when we saw his wife Gwen, another longtime teacher, his daughter Hope, as well as his son Gus, who captured so many hearts with his emotion in saying, "That's my dad." But while we're talking about the nerves and, and all the debates, this is somebody who's debated multiple times for when it was Congress, when it was, as a governor. And also, he used to host debate nights for high school teachers to talk about current events, so he has a little experience.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And don't underestimate high school debate teams, too. If, if you go to the high school debate team, you kind of know what you're doing.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly, yes.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the meantime, though, JD Vance, and again, it's sort of like the, the battle of as I said, the Midwestern dads but they have completely different backgrounds.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Exactly right, but also both veterans, both from rural America, happens that Vance is from Middletown, Ohio, really kind of had this hardscrabble childhood, which wrote about, of course, in his bestselling book "Hillbilly Elegy." But it was at the Republican National Convention this summer, where when he took the stage, he said, "I will be a vice president who never forgets where he came from." Vance served in the Marines, ultimately went to Yale for law school, became a venture capitalist and ultimately, now Ohio's freshman Senator.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But at 40 years old, he's actually the first millennial on a major party ticket. His wife, Usha, of course, he met at Yale Law School. She apparently has been helping to prep him for this debate tonight. They have three children together. And, and Vance, of course, as many people know was at one time a harsh critic of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but he says ultimately that Trump won his over strictly by his performance in office.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And Linsey, let me take that, that point back over to Rachel, because you said JD Vance is ready tonight. Is he ready on all of the, the past criticisms of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ? And it's not just, sort of, a light critique either. I mean, he, he was very obvious in, in sort of how he felt about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2016. And then, even after \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's first presidency, he had some tough words for him.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, brutal, I think, is the wo