 \par \uc2 PIERRE THOMAS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, new data from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  shows violent crime dropping dramatically. According to the \uc2 FBI\uc2 , murders fell a stunning 11 percent last year. That's the biggest one-year decline in 20 years. Also down, rape, assault and property crime like burglary and larceny and there's evidence this trend is continuing. According to preliminary estimates provided by the \uc2 FBI\uc2  on Monday, the number of violent crimes and property crimes are down big again this year. This is very similar to data we're seeing from the nation's major police departments. Law enforcement officials say this is real progress but admit more work needs to be done, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. We see how they tackle the issue tonight, the two vice presidential candidates. Again, we're 13 minutes away from the Vice Presidential Debate. Pierre Thomas, thank you. Before we go to break here, real quick to Rachel Scott, because reproductive rights also a huge issue nationally.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Both of these campaigns are tackling it in very different ways, obviously. But which of the states and, and how many of them are battleground states where people will be going to the polls not only in the Presidential race but also on the issue of reproductive rights?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATES WHERE ABORTION IS ON THE BALLOT IN NOVEMBER\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Abortion rights is gonna be on the ballot in as many as ten states this election including some battleground states, Nevada, Arizona and all eyes on Florida. Yes, this is a red state. Florida Governor \uc2 Ron Desantis\uc2  very popular here. There's a six-week abortion ban in this state. But Democrats believe that being on the ballot now puts this in play for them, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\