ll ready for some music? Do you want to hear some music? Rachel Platten is going to perform live when we come back here on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241010eka10003k\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:30 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 254 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STRIKE, DOCKWORKERS, VELOZ, DAGGETT, RHEE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, OWENBY, NORWOOD, CRISWELL, RAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESPERATE SEARCH & RESCUE MISSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELENE'S DEATH TOLL RISES WITH HUNDREDS STILL UNACCOUNTED FOR\par \par \uc2 STORM, TRACK, HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW TROPICAL THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE STORM FORMING THAT COULD HIT THE GULF COAST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BIDEN, HARRIS, HURRICANE HELENE, ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDIDATES RESPOND TO HURRICANE DISASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS BRIEFED BY FEMA OFFICIALS; PRESIDENT BIDEN BLASTS TRUMP COMMENTS\par \par \uc2 WALZ, VANCE, DEBATE, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO THE VICE PRESIDENTIAL DEBATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO EXPECT WHEN WALZ & VANCE FACE OFF TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 HEZBOLLAH, ISRAEL, BIDEN, NETANYAHU, HAGARI\par \par \uc2 ROSE, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BASEBALL GREAT PETE ROSE PASSES AWAY AT 83\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MLB'S ALL-TIME HITS LEADER WAS BANNED FOR GAMBLING ON THE GAME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, JOHNSON, BONE CANCER, SHIP\par \par \uc2 KORS, MERGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LUXURY MERGER LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FTC\uc2  FIGHTS PLAN TO BRING UPSCALE FASHION BRANDS TOGETHER\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, SALES FORECAST, SHOPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY SHOPPING SALES FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHEN & WHERE TO SCORE THE BIGGEST DEALS\par \par \uc2 KNUDSEN, BREAST CANCER, STATISTICS, REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS ON BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY RELEASES NEW STATISTICS REPORT\par \par \uc2 JONES, MARQUEZ, WEDDING, HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWER IN PINK, 8:14\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKERS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 CARTER, 100, PRESIDENT\par \par \uc2 FOOTBALL, LIONS, SEAHAWKS, DOLPHINS, TITANS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, STONE, TEROU, STOKELY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, KNUDSEN, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER AWARENESS MONTH\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Welcome back to "GMA" live from Times Square.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241010eka10003h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CANDIDATES RESPOND TO HURRICANE DISASTER HARRIS BRIEFED BY FEMA OFFICIALS; PRESIDENT BIDEN BLASTS TRUMP COMMENTS\b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STRIKE, DOCKWORKERS, VELOZ, DAGGETT, RHEE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, OWENBY, NORWOOD, CRISWELL, RAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESPERATE SEARCH & RESCUE MISSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELENE'S DEATH TOLL RISES WITH HUNDREDS STILL UNACCOUNTED FOR\par \par \uc2 STORM, TRACK, HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW TROPICAL THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE STORM FORMING THAT COULD HIT THE GULF COAST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BIDEN, HARRIS, HURRICANE HELENE, ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDIDATES RESPOND TO HURRICANE DISASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS BRIEFED BY FEMA OFFICIALS; PRESIDENT BIDEN BLASTS TRUMP COMMENTS\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) As Faith reported, the Biden administration supplied money and material to the storm zone. That didn't stop former President Trump from making false statements about the federal response as Vice President Harris cuts short a campaign to meet with FEMA officials. Rachel Scott is tracking the campaigns. Good morning, Rachel.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, George, good morning to you. Yeah, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  touched down in Georgia. He visited a part of this state that had been gutted by that storm. And despite vowing to put politics aside, he still resorted to pushing false claims about President Biden.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning, President Biden laying into \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  for pushing false claims that Georgia's Republican governor, \uc2 Brian Kemp\uc2 , could not get President Biden on the phone after the devastating storm despite the President providing full resources of the federal government to help.\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2  (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Let me give it to you straight. He's lying. And the governor told him he was lying. The governor told him he was lying. I have spoken to the governor. I spent time with him. And he told me he's lying. I don't know why he does this. And the reason I get so angry about it, I don't care what he says about me. But I care what he communicates to the people that are in need, implying that we're not doing everything possible. We are. We are.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Army placed officials and equipment in Georgia ahead of the storm. The federal government has deployed more than 3,500 people to Georgia and other states to respond to the aftermath. Still, this is what Trump said just hours earlier while surveying storm damage in southern Georgia.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 The governor is doing a very good job. He's having a hard time getting the President on the phone.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The reality, Kemp himself said he spoke with Biden.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR BRIAN KEMP (REP) (GEORGIA)\par \par \uc2 He just said, hey, what do you need? And I told him, you know, we got what we need. We'll work through the federal process. He offered that if there's other things we need just to call him directly, which I appreciate that.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Vice President Harris also changing her travel plans over the storm, canceling a campaign event in Nevada to return to Washington and meet with FEMA officials, saying she spoke to the governors of Georgia and North Carolina, too.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I plan to be on the ground as soon as possible. But as soon as possible without disrupting any emergency response operations because that must be the highest priority and the first order of business.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and President Biden saying that this is just the beginning when it comes to providing the full resources of the federal government, calling this storm one of the worst ever, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, Rachel, a judge had stepped in on Georgia's abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GEORGIA SIX-WEEK ABORTION BAN STRUCK DOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUDGE RULES THE LAW VIOLATES STATE'S CONSTITUTION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah. That judge ruling that Georgia's six-week abortion ban is unconstitutional. This ruling now allows abortions up here in Georgia until 20 weeks into a woman's pregnancy. This is likely only temporary. The state already vowing to appeal this. But it does put this issue back front and center in this battleground state with just 35 days to go until the November election, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Rachel Scott, thanks. Michael?\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, thank you, George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241010eka10002x\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:00 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STRIKE, DOCKWORKERS, VELOZ, DAGGETT, RHEE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, OWENBY, NORWOOD, CRISWELL, RAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESPERATE SEARCH & RESCUE MISSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELENE'S DEATH TOLL RISES WITH HUNDREDS STILL UNACCOUNTED FOR\par \par \uc2 STORM, TRACK, HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW TROPICAL THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE STORM FORMING THAT COULD HIT THE GULF COAST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BIDEN, HARRIS, HURRICANE HELENE, ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDIDATES RESPOND TO HURRICANE DISASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS BRIEFED BY FEMA OFFICIALS; PRESIDENT BIDEN BLASTS TRUMP COMMENTS\par \par \uc2 WALZ, VANCE, DEBATE, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO THE VICE PRESIDENTIAL DEBATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO EXPECT WHEN WALZ & VANCE FACE OFF TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 HEZBOLLAH, ISRAEL, BIDEN, NETANYAHU, HAGARI\par \par \uc2 ROSE, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BASEBALL GREAT PETE ROSE PASSES AWAY AT 83\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MLB'S ALL-TIME HITS LEADER WAS BANNED FOR GAMBLING ON THE GAME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, JOHNSON, BONE CANCER, SHIP\par \par \uc2 KORS, MERGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LUXURY MERGER LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FTC\uc2  FIGHTS PLAN TO BRING UPSCALE FASHION BRANDS TOGETHER\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, SALES FORECAST, SHOPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY SHOPPING SALES FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHEN & WHERE TO SCORE THE BIGGEST DEALS\par \par \uc2 KNUDSEN, BREAST CANCER, STATISTICS, REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS ON BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY RELEASES NEW STATISTICS REPORT\par \par \uc2 JONES, MARQUEZ, WEDDING, HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWER IN PINK, 8:14\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning America. It's 8:00 am. On strike. Tens of thousands of union dock workers at ports from Maine to Texas, hit the picket line. Now the standstill impacting the nation.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON STRIKE\par \par \uc2 DOCK WORKER (MALE)\par \par \uc2 Nothing's gonna move without us. Nothing.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 How it could cost the economy billions of dollars a week. What it could mean for supply chains and prices.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEIGHBORS HELPING NEIGHBORS\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Neighbors helping neighbors. The race to get relief into areas hard hit by Helene. People collecting water, food and supplies for those in need. Our friend, Yassin Terou, mobilizing his community again. This morning, what you can do to help.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Power in Pink. We're marking the beginning of Breast Cancer Awareness Month, with top experts sharing the latest on prevention, detection and treatment, and the importance of emotional support. Plus, recipes to help reduce your risk of cancer. Thrivers and caregivers are here, and they're saying...\par \par \uc2 THRIVERS AND CAREGIVERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Good morning America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning America. As that billboard shows you outside, we are kicking off National Breast Cancer Awareness Month this morning.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And we want to take a look at some beautiful thrivers out there and the unsung heroes we are going to sing about. We're talking about the caregivers. This morning we have the latest science and we're answering their questions and a whole lot more.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 That is coming up.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241010eka100039\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 NEW AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY REPORT ON BREAST CANCER LATEST ON SCREENING, TREATMENT & PREVENTION\b0\par\par\uc2 1,076 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STRIKE, DOCKWORKERS, VELOZ, DAGGETT, RHEE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, OWENBY, NORWOOD, CRISWELL, RAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESPERATE SEARCH & RESCUE MISSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELENE'S DEATH TOLL RISES WITH HUNDREDS STILL UNACCOUNTED FOR\par \par \uc2 STORM, TRACK, HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW TROPICAL THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE STORM FORMING THAT COULD HIT THE GULF COAST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BIDEN, HARRIS, HURRICANE HELENE, ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDIDATES RESPOND TO HURRICANE DISASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS BRIEFED BY FEMA OFFICIALS; PRESIDENT BIDEN BLASTS TRUMP COMMENTS\par \par \uc2 WALZ, VANCE, DEBATE, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO THE VICE PRESIDENTIAL DEBATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO EXPECT WHEN WALZ & VANCE FACE OFF TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 HEZBOLLAH, ISRAEL, BIDEN, NETANYAHU, HAGARI\par \par \uc2 ROSE, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BASEBALL GREAT PETE ROSE PASSES AWAY AT 83\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MLB'S ALL-TIME HITS LEADER WAS BANNED FOR GAMBLING ON THE GAME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, JOHNSON, BONE CANCER, SHIP\par \par \uc2 KORS, MERGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LUXURY MERGER LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FTC\uc2  FIGHTS PLAN TO BRING UPSCALE FASHION BRANDS TOGETHER\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, SALES FORECAST, SHOPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY SHOPPING SALES FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHEN & WHERE TO SCORE THE BIGGEST DEALS\par \par \uc2 KNUDSEN, BREAST CANCER, STATISTICS, REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS ON BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY RELEASES NEW STATISTICS REPORT\par \par \uc2 JONES, MARQUEZ, WEDDING, HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWER IN PINK, 8:14\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKERS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 CARTER, 100, PRESIDENT\par \par \uc2 FOOTBALL, LIONS, SEAHAWKS, DOLPHINS, TITANS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, STONE, TEROU, STOKELY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, KNUDSEN, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Morgan. Thanks very much. Turning now to Power in Pink. We are kicking off Breast Cancer Awareness Month with Dr. \uc2 Karen Knudsen\uc2 , the CEO of the \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2 , and ACS CAN. Welcome back. It's great to have you here. We want to talk about prevention screening and treatment right now. Let's start with screening. What are the latest guidelines?\par \par \uc2 DR \uc2 KAREN KNUDSEN\uc2  (CEO OF AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, so important. There's much science behind this. So it's important to know screening guidelines are for women of average risk. What does that mean? Starting at age 40, have that discussion with your physician about the right screening plan for you. All women should start their annual screening at age 45. After age 55, women have an option to stay with that annual screening or go to every other year until they have less than ten years to live. So even beyond age 75, if a woman has an expectation to live another ten years, she should still get screened.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What about younger women who don't qualify for a mammogram?\par \par \uc2 DR \uc2 KAREN KNUDSEN\uc2  (CEO OF AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, well, - it's important to understand that there is a rise in breast cancer in the younger population. They may below this 40. So if there's something that seems amiss, you must be screened. But also important to know who is not of average risk. Because risk is more than just about your age. It's your your genetics, your family history, your own medical health exposures. Those are the conversations to have as soon as possible with your doctor to understand what's the right screening plan for you.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And there really has been advancements in screening and advancements in treatment.\par \par \uc2 DR \uc2 KAREN KNUDSEN\uc2  (CEO OF AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. That's what's driving down this 44% reduction in breast cancer mortality that we reported on earlier today. Mammograms are not what they used to be. We used to be at two dimensional. Now we're at three dimensional. Much more effective for women whose breasts are difficult to image, like women who have dense breasts, who are at higher risk for breast cancer. Treatments have also improved. I'm old enough to remember when breast cancer was one disease. Now we know it's many subgroups that all arise due to different reasons and have to be treated with different therapies.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So many of us are learning for the first time about what is called preventive chemotherapy, after Princess Kate made her announcement. Explain what's going on there.\par \par \uc2 DR \uc2 KAREN KNUDSEN\uc2  (CEO OF AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY)\par \par \uc2 This is so incredibly important. There are thousands of women every year who go to mammography and they don't have breast cancer but are identified as having a high risk lesion or maybe they have a genetic risk of breast cancer. They can go on chemo prevention. The studies are quite clear for a large subgroup of these women. They can go on what's a low dose of tamoxifen or estrogen receptor related therapy that can significantly reduce their cancer risk. So beyond just the things you can do in your healthy living to reduce breast cancer risk, chemo prevention is real for breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And where do things stand on a breast cancer vaccine?\par \par \uc2 DR \uc2 KAREN KNUDSEN\uc2  (CEO OF AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY)\par \par \uc2 So vaccination against cancer is something not new to the cancer field. We know that we can effectively prevent many cancers through vaccination. For example, through vaccination against the human papilloma virus, for which we have the opportunity to eliminate, for example, cervical cancer. There's much now in clinical testing as well as in development for vaccinations that can help with breast cancer prevention, as well as therapeutic intervention. More to come.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's so important to hear. And we have a great group of thrivers and survivors and caregivers here.\par \par \uc2 DR \uc2 KAREN KNUDSEN\uc2  (CEO OF AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY)\par \par \uc2 Sure do.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In the studio. We'll be taking more questions from them later, but what's your most important message to everyone here?\par \par \uc2 DR \uc2 KAREN KNUDSEN\uc2  (CEO OF AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, I think the most important message is that there is more hope than ever before. Because of early detection, because of what we know we can do with prevention and because of advances in therapeutic intervention. So more to come, but certainly more hope than ever before.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And more to come here as well. We're going to continue our discussion with two other leading cancer experts, take questions from thrivers, survivors and caregivers right here in our studio. But now let's go to Ginger.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241010eka10003e\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 WEATHER\b0\par\par\uc2 444 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STRIKE, DOCKWORKERS, VELOZ, DAGGETT, RHEE, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, OWENBY, NORWOOD, CRISWELL, RAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DESPERATE SEARCH & RESCUE MISSION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HELENE'S DEATH TOLL RISES WITH HUNDREDS STILL UNACCOUNTED FOR\par \par \uc2 STORM, TRACK, HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW TROPICAL THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POSSIBLE STORM FORMING THAT COULD HIT THE GULF COAST\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , BIDEN, HARRIS, HURRICANE HELENE, ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDIDATES RESPOND TO HURRICANE DISASTER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS BRIEFED BY FEMA OFFICIALS; PRESIDENT BIDEN BLASTS TRUMP COMMENTS\par \par \uc2 WALZ, VANCE, DEBATE, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COUNTDOWN TO THE VICE PRESIDENTIAL DEBATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT TO EXPECT WHEN WALZ & VANCE FACE OFF TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 HEZBOLLAH, ISRAEL, BIDEN, NETANYAHU, HAGARI\par \par \uc2 ROSE, TRIBUTE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BASEBALL GREAT PETE ROSE PASSES AWAY AT 83\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MLB'S ALL-TIME HITS LEADER WAS BANNED FOR GAMBLING ON THE GAME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 QUEEN ELIZABETH II, JOHNSON, BONE CANCER, SHIP\par \par \uc2 KORS, MERGER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LUXURY MERGER LAWSUIT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FTC\uc2  FIGHTS PLAN TO BRING UPSCALE FASHION BRANDS TOGETHER\par \par \uc2 HOLIDAY, SALES FORECAST, SHOPPING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOLIDAY SHOPPING SALES FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHEN & WHERE TO SCORE THE BIGGEST DEALS\par \par \uc2 KNUDSEN, BREAST CANCER, STATISTICS, REPORT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS ON BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN CANCER SOCIETY RELEASES NEW STATISTICS REPORT\par \par \uc2 JONES, MARQUEZ, WEDDING, HURRICANE HELENE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POWER IN PINK, 8:14\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 DOCKWORKERS, STRIKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 CARTER, 100, PRESIDENT\par \par \uc2 FOOTBALL, LIONS, SEAHAWKS, DOLPHINS, TITANS\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, STONE, TEROU, STOKELY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COVER STORY\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, KNUDSEN, SCREENING\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Thanks, George. So glad we are getting into all of this. Let's talk about the heat in Phoenix. Another day, another record. They had their hottest all time September record on Saturday with 117. Today should have their hottest on record October temperature, going to 110. The heat has built back with this ridge all the way to San Francisco where the forecast is 94, which would be the first 90 degree temperature for downtown San Francisco in two years. So it's been a while since you've been this warm.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AUTUMN HEAT\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look at the excessive heat warnings still in place and the heat advisories that go up through Sacramento to nearly Redding there. That ridge isn't moving much. It's going to stick around. We've had that kind of blocked out pattern. Denver going to 90 could be a record. Phoenix stays at records for days and days. Look at this. Much warmer than normal.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEMPERATURES NEXT WEEK\par \par \uc2 GINGER ZEE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Utah, Nevada, all the way up to Montana for the next week or so. Let's get a check now a little closer to home.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NATIONAL MAP\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241010eka10003f\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THE INDEX\b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, BIDEN, AIRSTRIKE\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, IRAN, AIRSTRIKES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: U.S.: IRANIAN MISSILE BARRAGE "DEFEATED"\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, ISRAEL, HEZBOLLAH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDEAST CASTS SHADOW OVER VP DEBATE\par \par \uc2 STRIKE, DOCKWORKERS, VELOZ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PORT STRIKE COULD DRIVE PRICES HIGHER\par \par \uc2 HURRICANE HELENE, RESCUES, SEARCH, NORWOOD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT EFFORT TO HELP STORM VICTIMS\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, DUERR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MASSIVE MANHUNT FOR DANGEROUS ESCAPEE\par \par \uc2 BREAST CANCER, ROSE, AMOS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE INDEX\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) To "The Index," and to news on breast cancer tonight. Deaths from cancer declining in the US, breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The new concern, though, about a rise in cases among women under 50. The \uc2 American Cancer Society\uc2  says breast cancer rates have steadily climbed 1% a year over the last decade.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PETE ROSE, 1941 - 2024\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, the death of Pete Rose. The medical examiner revealing he died from natural causes, suffering from heart disease and diabetes.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The last pictures right here taken of Rose show him in Nashville just two days ago on Sunday surrounded by his former \uc2 Cincinnati Reds\uc2  teammates.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JOHN AMOS, 1939 - 2024\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Actor John Amos has died.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Best known for his roles in "Good Times," "Roots," "The West Wing," "Coming to America." John Amos was 84.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) When we come back here tonight, the images just in, former President Jimmy Carter in his blue cap, what he witnessed on this, his 100th birthday.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241003eka100030\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 ECONOMY AND IMMIGRATION FORMER PRESIDENT CAMPAIGNS IN GEORGIA\b0\par\par\uc2 814 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TROPICAL STORM HELENE, FLOODING, TRACK\par \par \uc2 CHEMICAL LEAK, EVACUATION, SIEFKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOUSANDS EVACUATING TOXIC TRAIN LEAK\par \par \uc2 HEZBOLLAH, ISRAEL, AIRSTRIKES, LEBANON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ISRAEL STRIKES BEIRUT AS FIGHTING RAGES\par \par \uc2 TRUMP, HARRIS, ELECTION, IMMIGRATION, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ECONOMY AND IMMIGRATION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Meanwhile, in the race for the White House, 42 days to go until the election. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  on the economy and on immigration this week. Former President Trump in Georgia, Vice President Harris headed to Pennsylvania, and then to the border in Arizona. And the new polling tonight, several new national polls showing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  with a slight edge over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but within the margin of error. And in the key battleground states, several states with \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  with a slight edge, others with \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  with the edge. This is a very close race. Here's Rachel Scott.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FORMER PRESIDENT CAMPAIGNS IN GEORGIA\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, in battleground Georgia, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  zeroing in on the top issue for voters, the economy. Promising that, if he wins, the US will scoop up manufacturing jobs from other countries.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 We're going to take their factories. American workers will no longer be worried about losing your jobs to foreign nations. Instead, foreign nations will be worried about losing their jobs to America.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump says he'll bring business back home by slashing taxes and regulations, and by imposing sweeping tariffs on foreign imports, something Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says will drive up prices on everything from groceries to gas to medicine. Many economists agree with her. And today, the Senate's top Republican says he does, too.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR MITCH MCCONNELL\uc2  (REP-KY) (SENATE MINORITY LEADER)\par \par \uc2 I'm not a fan of tariffs. They raise the prices for American consumers.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Vice President's team pointing to the more than 700,000 manufacturing jobs created during the Biden-Harris administration. Harris today leaning into what's become a defining issue for her campaign, abortion, saying she wants to abolish the Senate filibuster to restore reproductive rights as they existed under Roe versus Wade with a simple majority vote instead of the two-thirds vote now required.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I've been very clear. I think we should eliminate the filibuster for Roe and get us to the point where 51 votes would be what we need to actually put back in law the protections for reproductive freedom.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Trump has boasted of nominating three of the Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe versus Wade. Keenly aware he's paid a political price with female voters, the former President now making an all-out appeal to the women who are concerned about abortion rights.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REP) (PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I am your protector. I want to be your protector. As president, I have to be your protector. You will no longer be abandoned, lonely, or scared. You will no longer be in danger. You're not going to be in danger any longer. You will no longer have anxiety from all of the problems our country has today. You will be protected, and I will be your protector. Women, women will be happy, healthy, confident, and free. You will no longer be thinking about abortion. That's all they talk about. Abortion.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But tonight, a Harris campaign spokeswoman with a blunt response, "After ripping away our reproductive freedom, now he's trying to tell us how to think."\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, let's bring in Rachel Scott here with us. A rare moment in studio in New York instead of on the campaign trail. We so appreciate your long hours on the campaign trail. So, we've got former President Trump in Georgia on the economy. We've got Vice President Harris going to Pennsylvania on the economy, and then she's going to Arizona to the border.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Both of these candidates keenly aware that immigration and the economy are top issues to voters. So, first, Harris will be delivering that speech on the economy in Pittsburgh.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And then, she travels to battleground Arizona with a visit to our southern border. She's expected to tout the Biden administration's executive action that led to a significant drop in the number of migrants crossing the border. She's also expected to say that she would sign that bipartisan border bill into law that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  urged Republicans to reject, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) If she's elected. All right, Rachel Scott here with us in New York. Rachel, great to have you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020241001ek9o00005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SCANDAL ROCKS TRUMP-BACKED LT GOVERNOR ROBINSON DEMOCRATS SEIZE ON CONTROVERSY, FORMER PRES HAS YET TO PULL SUPPORT\b0\par\par\uc2 1,152 \uc2 words\par \uc2 21 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , ROBINSON, HARRIS, PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION\par \par \uc2 GEORGIA, VOTING, RULES\par \par \uc2 HEZBOLLAH, AIR STRIKE, LEBANON\par \par \uc2 FLASH FLOODING, SEVERE WEATHER\par \par \uc2 JUDGE, SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 SECRET SERVICE, TRUMP, ASSASSINATION ATTEMPT\par \par \uc2 SUBWAY SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 FAA\uc2 , AIRPORT, CRASH\par \par \uc2 EASTERN EQUINE ENCEPHALITIS, EEE\par \par \uc2 OHTANI, MLB, RECORD, 50-50 CLUB\par \par \uc2 FILM CLIP OF "TRANSFORMERS ONE"\par \par \uc2 "COLLEGE GAMEDAY"\par \par \uc2 PRESIDENTIAL ELECTION, TRUMP, HARRIS, ROBINSON, DEWINE\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right. Welcome back here to "GMA." As the clock ticks down to election day, just 45 days away, can you believe it? Joining us now are ABC multiplatform reporter Jay O'Brien and NPR White House correspondent and ABC News contributor Asma Khalid. Welcome to you both. Good morning. Hey, Jay, we've got several issues happening at the same time in some key states. We've got that North Carolina scandal, the GOP candidate for governor there reportedly posting on adult websites. He's denied it, but then you also have Ohio's GOP governor condemning those Trump comments on Haitian immigrants. Could this hurt Republicans?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SCANDAL ROCKS TRUMP-BACKED LT GOVERNOR ROBINSON\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATS SEIZE ON CONTROVERSY, FORMER PRES HAS YET TO PULL SUPPORT\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, Gio, in politics you never want to be playing defense. You always want to be playing offense. And these are two stories that just as a matter of a week or so have caused Republicans to, A, have to play defense, and even cause divisions among some Republicans. There are Republicans on the Mark Robinson story that said if that CNN report is true, those allegations against Robinson would be, quote, unquote, "damning." And then, of course, on the flip side, as you mentioned \uc2 Mike DeWine\uc2 , that brewing kind of drip, drip, drip of Republicans coming out and saying that these allegations about Haitian immigrants eating pets in Springfield, Ohio are also inappropriate.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OHIO GOVERNOR DEWINE PENS OP-ED\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CONDEMNING TRUMP FOR COMMENTS ABOUT HAITIAN IMMIGRANTS\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) DeWine in that op-ed called out Trump and Vance directly, saying that he's saddened that they continue to perpetrate these false claims. Point being, they've caused division amongst Republicans. The Trump campaign is not really responding, not doing the traditional political thing of trying to course correct or respond to all of this. Instead, they're just pursuing forward and letting Trump, in a way, be Trump.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Jay, thank you for that. Asma, want to bring you in. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ' big push on the campaign trail has really been focusing on reproductive rights. So talk to us about whether that's an important campaign strategy for her.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VP HARRIS FOCUSES ON REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS AS CRITICAL ISSUE\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, I would say from her campaign standpoint it is really central to their message, in major part because polls show that voters trust Harris more on issues of reproductive rights, abortion, than they trust \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 . You know, I was out with Harris the other night, Thursday night, when she sat down with \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2 , and in the audience there was the mother and sister of this young woman in Georgia who died recently because of complications from an abortion after that state's abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And there were women, I will tell you, in the audience, wiping away tears. The Harris campaign believes that abortion is an issue where they can attract independent leaning voters, Republican women, and the reason they think that is because in every state where abortion has been put directly to voters since Roe versus Wade was overturned, voters have chosen to expand abortion rights. So it's something you saw her lean into in Georgia yesterday. They've got this reproductive rights bus tour going around. It is an issue they believe it is one of their most compelling.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, Jay, let's go back to you and touch on the economy. Of course, another huge issue that had been leaning in Trump's favor in the polls recently, but Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  appears to be tightening the gap a little bit.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STATE OF THE RACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CANDIDATES & THE ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 JAY O'BRIEN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Absolutely, Whit. There was a new AP/NORC poll out just yesterday that shows 43 percent of respondents said they trust Trump to handle the economy, 41 percent Harris. And while Trump's got just a few point edge, it's a statistical tie pretty much, that shows that Vice President Harris has shaken up this race on this issue since \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was at the top of the ticket. The ABC News/Ipsos, we did a poll in May when \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was the Democratic nominee and Trump beat Biden on the economy by 14 points. That is just another sign of how different this race is, and another sign of just, frankly, how close it will come down to.\par \par \uc2 GIO BENITEZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, Jay, incredible to see how close it's coming as we get closer and closer to the election. All right, Asma. In his last few months in office, President Biden is really looking to cement his legacy. What's he focusing on right now?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT BIDEN'S FINAL MONTHS IN OFFICE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT HE'S FOCUSING ON AS HE LOOKS TO CEMENT HIS LEGACY\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Well, really, one aspect that a lame duck president can really focus on a lot, and that's what President Biden is seeing these days as, is foreign policy. And you're going to see him do that over the next several days. He's in Wilmington, his hometown today, inviting the leaders of Japan, Australia and India for this partnership known as The Quad. It's really seen as an attempt to counterbalance China's influence in the region.\par \par \uc2 ASMA KHALID (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Then President Biden will be at the \uc2 UN General Assembly\uc2 , later this week outlining his vision for the world, meeting with the president of Ukraine, \uc2 Volodymyr Zelenskyy\uc2 . You know, really, I will say centrally Biden is a man whose political career was based a lot on him being a foreign policy guy. The challenge for him is that there are multiple conflicts around the globe. Ukraine, obviously the war in the Middle East, that remain unresolved with no easy solution, and he's leaving office soon.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Asma Khalid and Jay O'Brien, thank you both so much for joining us this morning. Still coming up here on "GMA," why you might want to bring your pickle ball racket the next time you head to the movie theater.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241009ek9l0000g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 OPRAH HOSTS VIRTUAL RALLY FOR HARRIS VICE PRESIDENT ANSWERS VOTER QUESTIONS DURING STAR STUDDED EVENT\b0\par\par\uc2 1,054 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR MIDEAST ESCALATION\par \par \uc2 ISRAEL, HEZBOLLAH, STRIKES, DEAD, INJURED, MILL\par \par \uc2 WINFREY, HARRIS, RALLY, VOTERS, TRUMP, EMHOFF\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Marcus, thank you so much for that. We're gonna turn now to the race for the White House. And overnight, Vice President Harris was in Michigan with Oprah, fielding questions from voters, while former President Trump spoke at an anti-Semitism event in Washington, DC. Chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce is in Detroit for us with the latest. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: OPRAH HOSTS VIRTUAL RALLY FOR HARRIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VICE PRESIDENT ANSWERS VOTER QUESTIONS DURING STAR STUDDED EVENT\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Hey, Michael, good morning. Well this event here overnight in Michigan was signature \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2 , from the celebrity appearances to the deeply personal and emotional stories of voters. Harris and Oprah, well aware this race is extremely close, and trying to reach out to those key voters that will make all the difference.\par \par \uc2 OPRAH WINFREY (UNITED FOR AMERICA HOST)\par \par \uc2 Unite for America.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Overnight, the queen of talk, lending her star power to boost \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and get out the vote, hoping to reach the critical sliver of voters that will determine this race.\par \par \uc2 OPRAH WINFREY (UNITED FOR AMERICA HOST)\par \par \uc2 Please welcome \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In a highly produced virtual rally, Oprah trying to harness enthusiasm for Harris, and keep her momentum going, urging Americans to vote their values.\par \par \uc2 OPRAH WINFREY (UNITED FOR AMERICA HOST)\par \par \uc2 Let me tell you, it is about character, and it's about decency and respect, and all the things that we were raised to believe about what it means to be an American citizen and pursue the American dream.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Harris, doing something she rarely does, fielding questions directly from voters about the issues top of mind for them, from immigration, to the cost of living to reproductive rights.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The former President chose three members of the \uc2 United States Supreme Court\uc2 , with the intention that they would overturn the protections of Roe V Wade. And they did as he intended.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Speaking out for the first time, the family Amber Thurman. The 28 year old mother who is reportedly the first publicly known woman to lose her life as a result of Georgia's abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 SHANETTE WILLIAMS (MOTHER OF AMBER THURMAN)\par \par \uc2 You're looking at a mother that is broken. The worst pain ever that a mother, that a parent could ever feel.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) According to "\uc2 Pro-Publica\uc2 ," after a medical abortion, Amber suffered from a grave infection, but doctors waited 20 hours to operate, by then it was too late.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I am just so sorry. The word over and over again in her mind is preventable.\par \par \uc2 OPRAH WINFREY (UNITED FOR AMERICA HOST)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 So is she on death's door before you actually decide to give her help?\par \par \uc2 OPRAH WINFREY (UNITED FOR AMERICA HOST)\par \par \uc2 That's the problem. That's the problem.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Is that what we're saying?\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And on the issue of gun violence, Oprah noting Harris herself is a gun owner.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I'm a gun owner too. Walz in a gun owner.\par \par \uc2 OPRAH WINFREY (UNITED FOR AMERICA HOST)\par \par \uc2 I did not know that.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 If somebody breaks in my house, they're getting shot. Sorry.\par \par \uc2 OPRAH WINFREY (UNITED FOR AMERICA HOST)\par \par \uc2 Yes, yes, I hear that. I hear that.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Probably should not have said that. But, my staff will deal with that later.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP SPEAKS AT ANTISEMITISM EVENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHIC: FORMER PRESIDENT ATTACKS JEWS WHO SUPPORT DEMOCRATS & VP HARRIS\par \par \uc2 OPRAH WINFREY (UNITED FOR AMERICA HOST)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Back in Washington, former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  joining one of his top donors, Miriam Adelson, at an event aimed at fighting Anti-Semitism.\par \par \uc2 FMR PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 If we don't win this election, Israel in my opinion, within a period of two to three years will cease to exist, it's gonna be wiped out.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The former President has said Harris, quote, "Doesn't like Jewish people" and repeatedly attacked Jews who support Democrats and Harris.\par \par \uc2 FMR PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Any Jewish person that votes for her, epically now, her or the Democrat Party should have their head examined.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Harris' husband, Second Gentleman Doug Emhoff, himself Jewish, responding in an interview with our Michael Strahan.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He said this, quote, "She doesn't like Jewish people," and you...\par \par \uc2 SECOND GENTLEMAN DOUG EMHOFF (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 She likes me.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \u8230\'20\'26you're Jewish-American, so what was your reaction when you heard that in real time?\par \par \uc2 SECOND GENTLEMAN DOUG EMHOFF (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 So, it's typical \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  gas lighting. He is somebody who has had dinner with known Anti-Semites. He is somebody who during, after the horrific events of Charlottesville, where people actually marching with Tiki torches saying "Jews shall not replace us," and he said there were fine people were on both sides of that.\par \par \uc2 SECOND GENTLEMAN DOUG EMHOFF (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 This is a guy who has had a record of saying incredibly vile, Anti-Semitic things. So for him to say that, I just almost laugh at the hutzpah, as we would say. Abdu it's gas lighting.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Harris now heads to Georgia today for a big abortion speech in Atlanta. She'll again be highlighting Amber's story, and the very real consequences of what she calls Trump's abortion bans. She then finishes the day in battleground Wisconsin. Trump is off the trail today, but back out in North Carolina tomorrow. Michael.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Mary, thank you so much. We're gonna have more on my exclusive interview with Second Gentleman Dough Emhoff in our next half hour. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020241008ek9k00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HARRIS DEFENDS REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS HIGHLIGHTS GA MOTHER'S DEATH AFTER STATE'S ABORTION BAN\b0\par\par\uc2 833 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, ABORTION, THURMAN, ELECTION\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good evening. And it's great to have you with us as we year the end of another week together here. We'll have more on that judge shot and killed in the courthouse. Authorities tonight now say it was the sheriff who killed him, and what we've learned.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING NEWS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RACE FOR THE WHITE HOUSE\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But we do begin tonight with the race for the White House. Forty-six days to go to the election, and the fierce fight tonight in the key battlegrounds.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in Atlanta, her emotional comments today about the death of a mother who she says could not get care in time after reports medical help was delayed because of that state's strict abortion ban. The major headline also from Georgia tonight, that state's election board ordering the hand-counting of all ballots, likely delaying results on election night in what could already be a very close election. And former President Trump soon heading to the must-win state of North Carolina as scandal now swirls around the Republican candidate for governor in that state, \uc2 Mark Robinson\uc2 , who Trump has praised as better than \uc2 Martin Luther King Jr.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Mary Bruce leading us off with late developments in the race for president.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS DEFENDS REPRODUCTIVE RIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGHLIGHTS GA MOTHER'S DEATH AFTER STATE'S ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in battleground Georgia, a state that is putting a new spotlight on one of her campaign's key issues, abortion.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 This is a health care crisis, and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the architect of this crisis.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has boasted of appointing three of the Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe v. Wade. Georgia then implemented a law banning abortion at six weeks, before most women even know they're pregnant. Harris today shining a light on the death of 28-year-old mother Amber Thurman, pointing to a \uc2 ProPublica\uc2  report saying she is the first woman known to lose her life as a result of Georgia's abortion ban.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 We will speak her name, Amber Nicole Thurman. Amber Nicole Thurman.\par \par \uc2 SUPPORTERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Amber Nicole Thurman.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) After a medication abortion out of state was incomplete, Thurman suffered a grave infection. Her doctors waited 20 hours to operate. By then, it was too late, and she died. Overnight, Harris meeting with Thurman's mother at an event hosted by \uc2 Oprah Winfrey\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MOTHER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 I want you all to know, Amber was not a statistic. She was loved by a family, a strong family. And we would have done whatever to get my baby, our baby, the help that she needed.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I'm just so sorry.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Today, Harris blasting Trump and his running-mate, Senator \uc2 JD Vance\uc2 , as hypocrites.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The other folks, Trump and his running mate, and they'll talk, "Oh, yeah. But I, you know, I do believe in the exception to save the mother's life." Okay, all right, let's break that down. Shall we? Let's break that down. We're saying that we're going to create public policy that says that a doctor, a health care provider, will only kick in to give the care that somebody needs if they're about to die. Think about what we are saying right now.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Harris arguing Thurman's death may be the first we are hearing of, but it won't be the last.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 We knew this could happen. There is a word, preventable. And there is another word, predictable.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So, let's bring in Mary Bruce with us again tonight. Mary, the Vice President, of course, in Georgia as you reported there today, now headed to Wisconsin. I know there was another major headline out of Georgia as well today. This key ruling from the state election board?\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) David, the Georgia State Election Board today, in a move spearheaded by Trump supporters, approved a ruling requiring that all ballots cast on election day be counted by hand in addition to the customary machine count. Now, this is expected to be challenged in court. But if this holds, it could lead to a chaotic count and would certainly delay results in the critical state well beyond election night. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) In a very close presidential race already. Mary Bruce leading us off here. Mary, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020240926ek9k00002\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 MASSACHUSETTS GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY HARRIS CAMPAIGN PROMOTES UNITY-FOCUSED CLOSING STATEMENT\b0\par\par\uc2 2,136 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: This Week\par \uc2 THWK\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2024 American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK\par \par \uc2 DEBATE, 538, TRUMP, HARRIS, VOTERS, BRYANT, BOBIAK, MUHAMMAD, DEWINE, HAITIANS\par \par \uc2 HEALEY, HARRIS, DEBATE, IPSOS, MILITARY, ABORTION, ECONOMY\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM TUESDAY\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (2024 DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 As a prosecutor, I never asked a victim or a witness, are you a Republican or a Democrat? The only thing I ever asked them, "Are you okay?" And that's the kind of president we need right now. Someone who cares about you and is not putting themselves first. I intend to be a president for all Americans.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS CAMPAIGN PROMOTES UNITY-FOCUSED CLOSING STATEMENT\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  making her closing argument at Tuesday's debate on ABC. I'm joined now by Massachusetts Governor \uc2 Maura Healey\uc2 , clearly a supporter of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . You know, Democrats said quickly that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  won the debate. In fact, our poll found 58 percent of the voters thought she was the clear winner, and yet that performance did not overall move the needle. They're, they're basically in the same place as before the debate. Does that surprise you?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC/IPSOS POLL: HARRIS KEEPS SOLID LEAD NATIONALLY POST-DEBATE\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 No, not at all. I, Martha, we know that this is going to be a close race, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  says that she's an underdog. But what's important is that she and \uc2 Tim Walz\uc2  have built a campaign for a close race. They're opening an unbelievable number of offices around the country, tons of staff, tons of volunteers. The enthusiasm has been really strong. And I think what's very important also, is that she and Tim are playing for every voter. They're going to red counties. They're going to red districts, right? Because, as she said in her closing argument, I'm gonna be a president for all Americans. You may not agree with me on everything, but I'm gonna be here for you and your family.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 And one thing that the debate demonstrated to me at least is that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is about you. She's about the American people. She's thinking about your family. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's just about himself. Remember, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  is the one who's out there saying she's gonna cut taxes for 100 million Americans. She's gonna provide a tax credit to families with children. She's gonna produce more housing around the country so we can lower housing costs. She's focused on lowering the cost of prescription drugs and groceries.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Governor, I, I...\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 What have we heard from \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , beyond, beyond the, the, the pets and the like?\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) So...\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 So, you know, the debate, we've moved on from the debate. It's about the campaign.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Governor, I, I want to go back to the debate because that was important, and I want to go through a few things that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  said. I want to ask you about her comments about the military. She said during the debate, this about the US military. Let's listen.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (2024 DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 As of today, there is not one member of the United States military who is in active duty in a combat zone in any war zone around the world. The first time this century.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABOUT 2,000 US TROOPS STILL BASED IN IRAQ, ANOTHER 900 IN SYRIA\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Our fact checkers found that to be false and I have a lot of experience in that area as well. There are currently 900 US military personnel in Syria, 2,500 US troops in Iraq. All have been under regular threat from drones and missiles for months. We also have action in the Red Sea. We also, every single day, the Navy SEALS, Delta Forces, special operators, can be part of any sort of deadly raid. So, why would she make that claim?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 Well, I think what's important here, Martha, is that \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  in contrast to \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , demonstrated herself to be commander in chief. We are in a world where there are all sorts of conflicts, and it's all the more reason we need somebody who's serious and who supports the military, and just remember, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's own...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But Governor, but Governor, excuse me, but she said there is not one member of the United States military who is in active duty in a combat zone. That is not true. You say she demonstrated her ability to be commander in chief, but did she not know about these people in Syria and Iraq? Why would she say that?\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 Look, that was a comment, that was a comment in a debate. I think the point that she was trying to make was a broader point. And of course, we have military in place all around the country. That's important. We're the United States of America. And \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , remember, is the person who stands with \uc2 NATO\uc2 , who supports our allies, who's working to bring countries together. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  stands with \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 . So, you know, I think that's what's really important. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , she respects our military. She respects our service members.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  calls them suckers and losers, and it's why \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's former military generals support \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . They say that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  shouldn't be anywhere near the Oval Office, and I think those are the points, Martha, that people need to understand. We live in a world of very serious times with serious consequences, and the actions of the next commander in chief matter. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  will be that commander in chief and lead us forward in freedom, working with others. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is interested in saddling up to dictators.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and Governor, Governor, I want to hit another, I, I want to stick to, Governor, I want to stick to, I want to stick to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  here. On abortion, Vice President Harris did not make clear whether she supports any restrictions on abortion. Currently, nine states and the District of Columbia have no gestational ban on abortions. Your state of Massachusetts has a ban on abortion after 24 weeks. Your state drew a line. Should she let people know where she stands, and draw some sort of line?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC/IPSOS POLL: MORE TRUST HARRIS ON ABORTION, HEALTH CARE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS DOES NOT SAY IF SHE FAVORS ANY RESTRICTIONS ON ABORTION\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 She already did, Martha. What she said is, let's go back to Roe, which by the way, contrary to what \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  says, nobody was asking to be overturned except for some segment. She's been clear. And I can tell you that because I myself, am a former prosecutor, former attorney general, very similar with abortion laws, and we both respect the right for people, first off, to make their own individual decisions about their body, and what they want to do. That's very important. Women and families should have that choice. That includes the choice not to have an abortion. But what \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has said is she wants to take us back to Roe, which allowed for abortion in certain circumstances.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TRUMP DEFLECTS AT DEBATE ON WHETHER HE'D SIGN ABORTION BAN\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is, you know, here's what's really important. He did not say the other day in the debate, that he would veto a national abortion ban, and, in fact, he supports abortion bans just like the Trump abortion ban that's on the ballot in Florida, and it's appalling. It's appalling what that means for women, for families, for their health. And, you know, that is a clear, clear distinction in this race.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  wants to bring us back to the Roe period where we had protections in place and access. We weren't jailing doctors. Women weren't bleeding out and afraid. Husbands and wives who wanted to, to have children, you know, were able to access and, and make the, the health care decisions that they need to be able to protect their ability to do so. Victims of, of rape and incest had relief. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to take all of that away. That issue is a clear difference.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS FRAMES ECONOMIC AGENDA AROUND BOOSTING MIDDLE CLASS\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Governor, I want, I want to move onto the economy. There, there, there is a clear difference there. Governor, I want to, in terms of the economy, Vice President Harris says she has a plan for lifting the middle class. But right now the middle class, but right now the middle class under the Biden-Harris administration, eggs are up 119 percent, bread up 25 percent, chicken up 25 percent, the median home price is up 39 percent. This is the Biden-Harris administration. And \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is leading on the economy and immigration. What are your people saying to you? You must hear that as a governor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP: THE POWERHOUSE ROUNDTABLE\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. And, and look, I try to explain to people as governor, here's how we got here, okay? We had COVID which Trump did not handle well. There had to be a huge infusion of money to save our small businesses and, and to help our, all of our states. Inflation rose as a result. And what's happened under the Biden-Harris administration is they've actually worked to bring down inflation. There is still work to do. What's important, Martha, going forward, is that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants to make permanent tax cuts for the ultra-wealthy among us, okay, which is only going to burden us with more debt.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABC/IPSOS POLL: MORE TRUST TRUMP ON ECONOMY, IMMIGRATION\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 He also wants to put on more tariffs, which are gonna raise consumer prices for all of us. In contrast, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has said, I'm gonna lay the foundation to see further reductions in the interest rates, which I think we'll see soon, and prices are going to come down. But you, you know...\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, Governor.\par \par \uc2 GOVERNOR MAURA HEALEY (DEM-MA) (HARRIS-WALZ CAMP NATL ADVISORY BD)\par \par \uc2 It is very unfair to, to start that in the middle of the movie when the Biden-Harris administration came in and were dealing with a lot. We have the strongest economy of any country in the world right now, and they are committed to making life more affordable for people on housing, drugs, groceries, and the like. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  isn't.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay. Thank you so much for joining us this morning, Governor. We appreciate your time and your comments.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Coming up, Trump says he won't debate again. Is that a mistake? The Powerhouse Roundtable takes that on when we come back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 VIDEO CLIPS FROM THURSDAY\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (2024 DEMOCRATIC PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I believe we owe it to the voters to have another debate. Because this election and what is at stake could not be more important.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (2024 REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 She immediately called for a second debate, which means that she was like a prize fighter that lost a fight. Because we've done two debates and because they were successful, there will be no third debate.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  striking down the possibility of another debate after \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  advocated for one. So, how will the candidates now get their messages out in these final tension-filled weeks before Election Day? Our Powerhouse Roundtable is standing by to take it all on. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document THWK000020240925ek9f00003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HIGH-STAKES DEBATE SHOWDOWN HARRIS & TRUMP FACE OFF FOR FIRST TIME\b0\par\par\uc2 1,219 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FACE TO FACE\par \par \uc2 DEBATE, HARRIS, TRUMP, FALLOUT, SPIN ROOM\par \par \uc2 DEBATE, HARRIS, TRUMP, ISSUES, POLL\par \par \uc2 HARRIS, TRUMP, DEBATE, REACTION, TRADE, UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 FRANCINE, RAIN, LANDFALL, GULF COAST, POWER\par \par \uc2 FRANCINE, LANDFALL, RAIN, WINDS, FLOODING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORM SURGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRES, CREWS, EVACUATIONS, RESIDENTS, ACRES, CONTAINMENT\par \par \uc2 CHRISTIE, BRAZILE, DEBATE, HARRIS, \uc2 TRUMP\par \par \uc2 DELTA, JETS, COLLISION, TAXIWAY, EDWARDS, WEEDEN\par \par \uc2 CUSTODIAN, FRANCIS, HIGH SCHOOLERS, \uc2 JEEP\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FIRE AND WIND ALERTS\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 , HARRIS, PRESIDENTIAL DEBATE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) First look at the top stories breaking at 8. We start with last night's presidential debate. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 /\uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  met for the first time. It began with Harris walking across the stage to shake the former president's hand. That kicked off 90 minutes of confrontation. Chief white house correspondent Mary Bruce starts us off here. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BREAKING AT 8\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FACE TO FACE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: 9/11 MEMORIAL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILDFIRE EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH-STAKES DEBATE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS & TRUMP FACE OFF FOR FIRST TIME\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning again, George. Well, it was a fierce 90 minutes on that debate stage last night. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  really putting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the defensive, repeatedly trying to get under his skin, goading the former president to go off message. And Trump took the bait, often allowing the personal attacks to overshadow much of the policy.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It started with what appeared to be a moment of civility. A historic handshake initiated by the Vice President. The rivals meeting for the very first time.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Let's have a good debate.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Nice to see you. Have fun.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Thank you.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But the niceties didn't last. Nominees quickly digging into each other, beginning with the issue top of mind for many voters, the economy.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  actually has no plan for you because he is more interested in defending himself than he is in looking out for you.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 She doesn't have a plan. She copied Biden's plan and it's like four sentences. Like run Spot run. Four sentences that just, oh, we'll try to lower taxes.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Vice President repeatedly goading \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , trying to get under his skin.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 What you will also notice is that people start leaving his rallies early out of exhaustion and boredom.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The former president taking the bait.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 She said people start leaving. People don't go to her rallies. There's no reason to go.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But Trump throwing the heat right back at her.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Wait a minute. I'm talking now, if you don't mind. Please. Does that sound familiar? She went out...\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) One of the most contentious exchanges of the night on abortion. Harris trying to capitalize on Democrats' advantage on the issue.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS & TRUMP CLASH OVER THE ECONOMY, ABORTION, BORDER & MORE\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 One does not have to abandon their faith or deeply held beliefs to agree the government and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  certainly should not be telling a woman what to do with her body.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She also dodged when asked if she would support any abortion restrictions, while Trump repeated false claims, prompting a fact check from moderator Lindsey Davis.\par \par \uc2 LINSEY DAVIS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There is no state in this country where it is legal to kill a baby after it's born.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And he refused to rule out signing a national abortion ban. On immigration, Trump trying to pin previous chaos at the border on Harris.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 They're destroying the fabric of our country by what they've done.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Harris laying into Trump for urging Republicans to kill the bipartisan border deal.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 But what we have in the former president is someone who would prefer to run on a problem instead of fixing a problem. And I'll tell you something, he's gonna talk about immigration a lot tonight even when it is not the subject that is being raised.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Less than two months until the election, Trump still refusing to concede he lost the last one.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Are you now acknowledging that you lost in 2020?\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 No, I don't, I don't say that at all.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But you said, sir...\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 I said that sarcastically. You know that.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But the...\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 It was said, oh, we lost by a whisker. That was said sarcastically. Look. There's so much proof. All you have to do is look at it. And they should have sent it back to the legislatures for approval.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The reality, there is no evidence of widespread voter fraud and President Biden won the 2020 contest. Harris using the moment to call Trump unqualified.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was fired by 81 million people. So let's be clear about that. And clearly he is having a very difficult time processing that. But we cannot afford to have a president of the United States who attempts, as he did in the past, to upend the will of the voters in a free and fair election.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) In their closing statements, Harris vowing to help take the country forward.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 I intend to be a president for all Americans and focus on what we can do over the next ten and twenty years to build back up our country by investing right now in you, the American people.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) While Trump finally honed in on his message, questioning why Harris hasn't accomplished her plans during her time as vice president.\par \par \uc2 FORMER PRESIDENT DONALD TRUMP (REPUBLICAN PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE)\par \par \uc2 They've had three-and-a-half years to create jobs and all the things we talked about. Why hasn't she done it?\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now the Harris campaign is certainly feeling good this morning. So much so, they are now challenging \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  to a second debate. We will see if we see that ultimately happen. But the question remains whether any of this moved the needle. Will it make a difference in this race? One voter who has been swayed, Taylor Swift, posting last night to her 283 million \uc2 Instagram\uc2  followers that she has made up her mind, endorsing \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Again, our thanks for you, Mary, for your reporting.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020240926ek9b0000g\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 HIGH STAKES DEBATE SHOWDOWN HARRIS & TRUMP FACE OFF FOR FIRST TIME\b0\par\par\uc2 1,763 \uc2 words\par \uc2 11 September 2024\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2024, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FACE TO FACE\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Harris clearly signaling there that she wanted to take command, kicking off 90 minutes of confrontation. Former President rump on defense for most of the night. And the first debate polls say that voters think Harris won. Our team is live in Philadelphia this morning. Chief White House correspondent Mary Bruce starts us off. Good morning, Mary.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HIGH STAKES DEBATE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HARRIS & TRUMP FACE OFF FOR FIRST TIME\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, George. Well this was a fierce and fiery face-off. \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on the defensive for much of the night. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  taking every chance she could to get under his skin, goading Trump to go off message, while avoiding much focus on her own vulnerabilities. The policy often overshadowed by these personal attacks. But the this morning, the big question remains, will any of this be enough to fundamentally change the dynamics of this race.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) It started with what appeared to be a moment of civility, a historic handshake initiated by the Vice President. The rivals meeting for the very first time.\par