eaking with along the border, they say as of right now things are quiet and manageable. And then you add to that the tighter asylum restrictions and then the summer heat and things are considerably different than what we saw in places like El Paso, where we're standing right now, in comparison to what we saw last year, right?\par \par \uc2 MIREYA VILLARREAL (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The thing about immigration is, it is an unknown for most of America and that generates a lot of fear in people, which is why this has become a very hot topic. When we saw Trump on the border in Arizona a few weeks ago he laid out part of his plan talking about tighter restrictions and penalties as part of what he wants to do if he's elected. On the other side of it, we haven't heard much from Harris when it comes to her immigration plan other than she would try and resurrect that border security bill that was torpedoed right now. Listen, we have talked to voters. They want facts. They want policy. They want strategy. Jon?\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And look, Trump's been taking a hard line on this issue for a long, long time but an even harder line this time than when he first ran.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, he is vowing mass deportations and in a recent interview he suggested that he would even use the National Guard, and even the military to target, we're talking about 15 million to 20 million people possibly. The last government estimate was 11 million migrants.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I mean, the logistics of that are beyond...\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Which he hasn't necessarily explained exactly how this would be carried out.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But it is one of the campaign promises that he makes over and over again at every single