y highway. These are all impacts on the way people actually feel, Jon.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, whatever the global stats are people are concerned about crime. Martha?\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, of course, another key issue, abortion, Mary, and, and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  looks at this as a, a very strong issue for the Democrats.\par \par \uc2 MARY BRUCE (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She has been out in front on this issue and hammering \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  on this, blaming him, pointing the finger squarely at him, saying he's to blame for the tough new abortion restrictions sweeping the country. We have seen over and over again that she notes that he has bragged about appointing the Supreme Court justices who overturned Roe. She knows that polling shows this is a, a winning issue for her, and of course that every time that abortion access has been on the ballot since Roe was overturned, reproductive rights have won. They see this as an issue that they hope will drive voters to the polls in November, especially as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has been really struggling to define his position.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA RADDATZ (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And, and he really has struggled to define that position. He takes credit for, for helping to overturn Roe v. Wade, but otherwise not very specific.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He has been all over the map on this issue. But when you look at his record and what he has done, he's appointed three of the five Supreme Court justices that overturned Roe versus Wade. That cleared the way for 22 states to either ban or severely restrict access to abortion. But Trump has also said, even though this is, he believes this should be a states' issue, he believes some have gone too far. He thinks the six- week abortion ban in Florida, for instance, his home state has gone too far.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \