ing to be, you know, a state that you can't take your eye off of. People in Michigan are good, hardworking people. We expect our leaders to be as good, if not better, and work just as hard if not harder. And it's always gonna be a close race.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) John Karl back with me here tonight. John and I were side by side last week at the Republican Convention. He was breaking news all week long. Back with us on this major turn in the race for President tonight and John, you know, you and I were talking, when you go down that list of potential running mates, and again, \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  still has to get the nomination officially, she says she's gonna earn that, but if and when that happens, then she has to choose a running mate.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) There's gonna be a lot of, sort of calculations as to who might benefit her most. But one of the most telling things, obviously about that list, Josh Shapiro, Pennsylvania, Roy Cooper, North Carolina, \uc2 Mark Kelly\uc2 , Arizona, \uc2 Gretchen Whitmer\uc2  at the end and what she said to George in recent days obviously from the very key battleground of Michigan, but John, I just wanted to read this to you because everyone's gonna be reading the tea leaves every hour, every day now. Less than a month until the Democratic National Convention.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight we've learned that Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  spoke with Pennsylvania Governor Josh Shapiro, someone whose name has come up with a possible vice presidential pick this afternoon. According to somebody familiar with the conversation, it's now been confirmed to ABC News. And again, she's also spoken with House Speaker, House Democratic Leader - \uc2 Hakeem Jeffries\uc2 , along with so many other Democratic leaders.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) But every conversation she has with somebody on this list of potential running mates, and of the names I just mentioned, obviously, Josh Shapiro right near the top of the list. First term governor in the state of, the key battleground state of Pennsylvania, a state that either side is going to have to win if they want to win the White House.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, absolutely and this shows this was one of the reasons why there was pressure on Biden not to run for reelection in the first place, because the party does have rising stars in, that happen to be sprinkled out in those key battleground states. Popular governors. Not just governors, members of the President's cabinet. \uc2 Gina Raimondo\uc2 , \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 . I mean, there's a lot of talent in the Democratic party ready to go out there.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And I think it was also notable, David, in addition to that phone call you just mentioned with Josh Shapiro, and by the way, I'm gonna say, we haven't heard yet, but I bet you that we will learn that there were several phone calls today. \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , I'm sure her phones were ringing and she was getting calls from a lot of those people we just mentioned. But look at the people that endorsed her today. Josh Shapiro, obviously, endorsed her. You mentioned that. Also, \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 , another name that had been mentioned, the Governor of California endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN KARL\uc2  (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) \uc2 Pete Buttigieg\uc2 , the Transportation Secretary, also thought as a potential, you know, rival to replace Biden and perhaps a vice presidential contender, as well. He endorsed \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  today. So, I think you're gonna see much more of this in the coming days, people reaching out to \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 , endorsing her and perhaps positioning to remind her that they could be a quality running mate.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 