ident, she's covered the issue of abortion rights across this country, and of course the overturning of Roe a couple of years ago now. And, of course, this big test today from the Supreme Court on abortion rights, testing the states rolling back these rights, issuing abortion bans across the country.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) The state of Idaho, the first one where this was tested, whether or not a woman who has a health risk going to the ER, should be allowed to get an abortion. And the Court saying today, Rachel, yes for now, sending it back down to the Courts. But the larger question going into tonight, how big of an issue will President Biden make this going into Election Day? And, and how will the former president, if this is President Biden's key issue or one of them, how will the former President, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , get up there and defend as he continues to do, putting in place the justices who overturned Roe in the Court?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are expecting President Biden to really drill in on this issue, David, because it is, of course, the former president who appointed three of the five Supreme Court justices that overturned Roe versus Wade. That cleared the way for 21 states to ban or severely restrict access to abortion. The President and Democrats looking at what's happening across the country, they are keenly aware that abortion rights has won in all six states where it has appeared on the ballot, even in Conservative states, Kansas, Kentucky, Ohio.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAP OF STATES: ABORTION RIGHTS IN AMERICA\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) It could be on the ballot in as many as a dozen states this November, including several critical battlegrounds. As for the former president, I am told that Trump's advisers have prepared him for questions about this, and especially on his stance on abortion bans going forward. We know the former president believe